8cef915f07575"} {"question" "e-4447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of $a_{13}$ in \n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/example-4447.json" "file_sha256" "e2b8e5b85cb998040a735ea24e82734f7ebea447097fa37c7c5a8e140239e291"} {"question" "e-4447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To get the minor of $a_{13}$, we remove the $1$st row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 1 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & ∗ & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & ∗ & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/example-4447.json" "file_sha256" "e2b8e5b85cb998040a735ea24e82734f7ebea447097fa37c7c5a8e140239e291"} {"question" "e-4448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the cofactor of $d_{23}$ in \n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/example-4448.json" "file_sha256" "b59eed74b5985bde3764a1be4405e5a88fc6bfd59d21306a0d95980af0c1dc29"} {"question" "e-4448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to get the minor of $d_{23}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & ∗ & -6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & -2 & ∗ \\\\ 6 & 0 & ∗ & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & ∗ & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of $d_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}{M}_{23} \\\\  & =-{M}_{23} \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/example-4448.json" "file_sha256" "b59eed74b5985bde3764a1be4405e5a88fc6bfd59d21306a0d95980af0c1dc29"} {"question" "e-4449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/example-4449.json" "file_sha256" "2f9b39c31065c50678299b03a48bcc83f6f37899d7d72b080b3c7b03efc8ca3b"} {"question" "e-4449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+2\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2{C}_{13} \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 1 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & ∗ & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & ∗ & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(5|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =2(5(6\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3)-(1\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-6))+0(1\\cdot 3-6\\cdot (-6))) \\\\  & =2(15+6+0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/example-4449.json" "file_sha256" "2f9b39c31065c50678299b03a48bcc83f6f37899d7d72b080b3c7b03efc8ca3b"} {"question" "q-71017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/ma